Skill: **Clone repository and run boundary scan** (Go / TypeScript / Java + **unit test inventory**).

## Runner goal

Spawn `clone-and-boundary-scan-runner` with spawn_contract goal verbatim.

## Script delivery (spawn context — mandatory)

Ubuntu sidecars are **shared** — per-run isolation: **`WORK_ROOT=/home/integration/.<workflow_run_id>/`**. Script pack is **embedded at tofu apply** (sidecar env) — the workflow never clones a tooling repo at runtime.

**Tool order:** `notes_index` → `read_notes` (for `github_repo_url`, `default_branch`) → **one** `execute_series`: prepend `export GITHUB_REPO_URL='<from read_notes>' DEFAULT_BRANCH='<branch>'` then paste **`SCAN_EXECUTE_SERIES_DECODE_COMMAND`** verbatim (single `$` only). **`create_files` is forbidden.**

Session `note()` alone does not write to `$WORK_ROOT/notes.json` on the sidecar — the runner must pass repo URL via those shell exports on the same line as the decode command.

## Test inventory capture (mandatory notes)

After scan, read `$WORK_ROOT/notes.json` and mirror:

- `test_inventory_attached=true`
- `test_confidence_score` (numeric from JSON)
- `test_frameworks` (comma-separated or JSON array string)
- `packages_without_tests` count or top-N list for analyst handoff
- `runtime_deps_provisioned=true` when Java/Go/Node were installed via apt
- `baseline_test_status` (`passed` | `failed` | `skipped`) and `baseline_test_run_evidence=true` when suite passed

**Never defer baseline tests** with "Java not available in runner env" — Ubuntu runners have root/sudo; the bootstrap installs required JDK/Go/Node from project signals (`.java-version`, Gradle/Maven, `go.mod`, `package.json`) then runs `test_inventory` recommended commands.

For large Gradle monorepos, set `note(key=baseline_test_command, value=./gradlew :module-a:test :module-b:test)` before spawn to override the default `./gradlew test`.

The scan populates:

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `test_inventory` | Per-language counts, frameworks, recommended commands |
| `test_frameworks` | Detected runners (`go_test`, `junit5`, `vitest`, `jest`, …) |
| `packages_without_tests` | Packages/workspaces lacking unit tests — split risk |
| `test_confidence_score` | 0–1 heuristic for analyst gating |

## Success criteria

- `boundary_scan_json_attached=true`
- `boundary_scan_json_path` under WORK_ROOT
- **`cce_summary`** in notes (compact: `cloud_by_provider`, `top_directories`, `critical_path_dirs` — never paste full entitlement arrays)
- `cce_plan.candidate_file_count` and `critical_path_dirs` inside `boundary_scan.json` (from `cce plan` + heuristics)
- `cloud_entitlements` / `cce_reports.*` inside `boundary_scan.json` (Tier-1 recipes: cloud, outbound coupling, platform adoption; lens add-on: monorepo intelligence, integration replatforming)
- `test_inventory_attached=true`
- `script_pack_version=${script_pack_version}`
- Final line: `stage_summary:clone-and-boundary-scan=ok` or `blocked:missing_github_repo_url`

## Blocked sentinels

- `blocked:missing_github_repo_url` — no clone (runner did not prepend `GITHUB_REPO_URL` from `read_notes`)
- `blocked:clone_failed` — auth/network
- `blocked:boundary_scan_failed` — scan script error
- `script_pack_error=runner_sha256_mismatch` — **sidecar env stale** (see README “Sidecar env drift”); escalate to platform/infra, then **new workflow run**
- `script_pack_error=*` — other embed verification or install failure
